From b9564952f5774b986f36f9ab10761b68348f3665 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:51:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(app): machine check reads a 4th-axis table's pose
 through the tool axis

On a machine whose only rotary turns about X (the 770MX + microARC 4),
the pose check judged the canonical letters one by one and refused the
face underneath, A0 B180, as "states no B axis" - although that table
reaches it as A180 and the PathPilot post (#785) already posts it so.

The pose gate moves to machine/judge.rs (pose_problems). On a machine
with exactly one rotary, stated along X, it reads the tool angle about X
from the letters with the post's own formula and tolerances
(tormach.cps toolAngle), signs it by the stated direction and judges it
against the travel. A pose with an X component (any B or C a turn about
X cannot make) is refused by name. Every other machine keeps the letter
law unchanged.

fanuc.cps writes the stream's letters as they come, so it now refuses a
turning letter with no rotary of that name. The A0 B180 the check now
passes on an A-only table can never reach that control as a B word.

Pinned by crates/app/tests/fourth_axis_pose.rs; the microARC wrap test
now expects the post's refusal (simultaneous 4-axis) instead of the
check's B180 one.

Fixes #797

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
